     "<div dir=\"ltr\">you could use anti_join between the old dataset and the new dataset, and present the outcome, which would only have records that appear on the new dataset and not the old.<br><br>See here:<br><a href=\"http://zevross.com/blog/2014/08/05/using-the-r-function-anti_join-to-find-unmatched-records/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://zevross.com/blog/2014/08/05/using-the-r-function-anti_join-to-find-unmatched-records/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496500455000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ce1oOAcrFrt8nSWRU6Heh\">http://zevross.com/blog/2014/08/05/using-the-r-function-anti_join-to-find-unmatched-records/</a><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
